# Carom — Balls, serving, and physics
{{#if (eq variant.slug "multi")}}

This file defines how the balls move and interact with the field — the physics
loop, collision, and the paddle bounce and spin mechanic — and, for this variant,
the three independent balls and how each is served. It builds on the geometry in
`specs/playfield.md` and the coordinate system in `specs/overview.md`.

## The balls

Three balls are in play at once. Each is the ball from `specs/playfield.md`, a
circle of radius 11 with serve speed 520 and a 1.04 speed multiplier per paddle
hit up to the 980 cap, and each carries its own velocity and its own spin scalar.
The physics below — stepping, collision, and the spin mechanic — apply to every
ball independently.

The three balls do not start, reset, or score as a group. Each ball is its own
independent contest: when one ball leaves the field it resets and relaunches on
its own while the other two keep playing without interruption.
{{else}}

This file defines how many balls are in play and how they are served, and how a
ball moves and interacts with the field: the physics loop, collision, and the
paddle bounce and spin mechanic. It builds on the geometry in
`specs/playfield.md` and the coordinate system in `specs/overview.md`.

## The ball

One ball is in play, the ball from `specs/playfield.md`: radius 11, serve speed
